# seed: 2
# requires: hero_ready map_enter battle_start battle_lost battle_hero_death hero_resurrect
# requires-match: battle_hero_death .*resurrect=1
# FUN_00494fcd: losing a fight. The hero takes a normal random encounter and never presses
# A, so the fight runs to the only end the original allows offline.
#
# With the solo auto-resurrect flag (DAT_00502a48) the local hero is not simply left at 0 HP:
# FUN_0042b6f3 gives the tenths of a level the hero had progressed, FUN_0042b765 writes the XP
# interpolated at THAT fractional level - so the progress toward the next level is what dies with
# it - and FUN_0042b6c1 recomputes the level from the reduced XP. The flag is then cleared, so the
# next death is a real one and front.c shows the death screen instead. FUN_00480875 and
# FUN_004946b2 have already banked the kills into the fight-scoped monster table.
#
# FUN_0041B891's own table (all.c:21078) has THREE states before the Well, not two:
#   1 main menu -> 2 "Where Do You Want To Play Today?" (splash, FUN_0041D31F)
#   2 -> 3 "Choose Your World" + the world list (FUN_0041D717)
#   3 -> take the highlighted row (msg 0x474) -> the Pick-a-Soul window
# RETURN is the plan's keyboard shortcut for the click.
#
# The Gateway of Dreams (map 0 link 0, SCENE 3) sits one cell south of the Evergreen
# spawn, and quest.txt:1774 makes its first visit an `ASK 30` -- the golden rule,
# "Do you agree to obey the golden rule? (type YES or NO)". An ASK suspends the scene
# until the player answers, so every script that walks into the link has to answer it
# the way a player does: Y (scene.c's ST_ASK sets the reply to "YES"). Left unanswered
# the scene waits forever and nothing downstream can fire. The Soul Brother also hands
# over L1 / H5000 / M5000 and a Ticket Home, opens the `OFFER2 0,10` shop, and sizes the
# trophy bag to 4x3, so this is a real visit and not a scripted cut to the fight.
expect boot_menu 900
# FUN_00402A73's Terms of Service modal opens on entry to the main menu (front.c:534
# tos_gate, consumed at front.c:770) and swallows the next key. "I Accept" is
# tos_accept = (356,371,75,23), so its centre is (393,382).
click 393 382
expect tos_accept 300
# State 2 is where FUN_0041F699 makes its synchronous 0x46F call, which raises
# SRNet's modal (0x42AA10). 1005 "Solo Game" is (250,313,299,23) -> centre
# (399,324); control 1 "Play Game" is (250,380,75,23) -> centre (287,391).
# 1005 then 1 closes it, 0x46F returns 1, FUN_0041D374 registers
# "--- Scanning ---", and the stepper FUN_00438E8E runs ~30 calls (6140 to
# 8340 ms) before FUN_0041B891(3) draws the world list.
# Main menu: RETURN is the Play-now shortcut (0x46B) into state 2.
key RETURN
wait 30
click 399 324
wait 10
click 630 309
wait 240
# State 3 is the world list; RETURN takes the highlighted row
# (msg 0x474), which is the keyboard shortcut for the row's click.
key RETURN
wait 30
key n
wait 5
text GapDeath
key RETURN
expect hero_ready 300
expect map_enter 600
# One cell south is the Gateway of Dreams, map 0 link 0 (x=179, y=219).
keydown DOWN
expect scene_enter 600
keyup DOWN
wait 40
key RETURN
wait 40
key RETURN
wait 40
key RETURN
wait 40
key y
wait 20
key RETURN
wait 40
key RETURN
wait 40
expect panel_open 600
key ESCAPE
wait 20
key RETURN
wait 20
key RETURN
wait 20
key RETURN
wait 20
key RETURN
wait 20
key RETURN
wait 20
key RETURN
wait 20
key RETURN
wait 20
key RETURN
wait 20
key RETURN
wait 20
key RETURN
wait 20
key RETURN
wait 20
key RETURN
wait 20
key RETURN
wait 20
key RETURN
wait 20
key RETURN
wait 20
key RETURN
wait 20
key RETURN
wait 20
key RETURN
wait 20
key RETURN
wait 20
key RETURN
wait 20
key RETURN
wait 20
key RETURN
wait 20
key RETURN
wait 20
key RETURN
wait 20
key RETURN
wait 20
key RETURN
wait 20
key RETURN
wait 20
key RETURN
wait 20
key RETURN
wait 20
key RETURN
wait 20
key RETURN
wait 20
expect map_enter 2000
# East past the Gateway's link rectangle (x=189 is still inside it, x=190 is not) and
# then south, until FUN_0046260E's per-tick roll hands the hero to SCENE 2.
hold RIGHT 60
expect hero_move 300
wait 20
keydown DOWN
expect encounter 2000
keyup DOWN
expect battle_start 600
# The hero never attacks: A is a queued action, nothing else is pressed, so the monster
# grinds a level-1 hero (20 HP) down to nothing on its own.
wait 12000
expect battle_hero_death 1500
expect hero_resurrect 600
expect battle_lost 600
expect map_enter 1200
quit
